### Pre-Commit Checklist

Before committing any solution, verify ALL of these:

- [ ] Class JavaDoc complete (all sections present)
- [ ] Problem link is valid and accessible
- [ ] Difficulty level matches source
- [ ] Minimum 2 topic tags included
- [ ] Company tags added if applicable
- [ ] Problem statement is clear
- [ ] Example with input/output provided
- [ ] Intuition has minimum 3 bullet points
- [ ] Approach has minimum 4 clear steps
- [ ] Time complexity documented with explanation
- [ ] Space complexity documented with explanation
- [ ] Minimum 3 edge cases documented
- [ ] All public methods have JavaDoc
- [ ] All helper methods documented
- [ ] @param tags for all parameters
- [ ] @return tags for return values
- [ ] Inline comments for complex logic
- [ ] Code follows naming conventions
- [ ] No unused imports
- [ ] No unused variables
- [ ] No magic numbers (or explained)
- [ ] No System.out.println debugging
- [ ] No commented-out code
- [ ] No TODO/FIXME comments
- [ ] Package declaration matches structure
- [ ] README updated with problem entry
- [ ] File compiles without errors
- [ ] No IDE warnings
- [ ] Alternative approaches included (if applicable)
- [ ] Trade-offs explained (if multiple approaches)

